papers/203-monochromatic-triangle-complementation/current_inputs/SOURCE_OWNER.md:40:| P147–151 combinatorial `Q01`, full focused section, and current replacement-lane `LFCTR` row | Same **generic minimum-involution selector**, already owner/thin-killed, but on cyclic directed triangles of tournaments. Its fixed locus is transitive tournaments and cyclic reversal preserves scores. MCT tests constant edge colours in a simple undirected graph; this is not that literal. A reinterpretation of bits as tournament orientations does not turn every constant triple into a directed cycle. No converse broad claim that triangle language alone separates systems is made. |
papers/203-monochromatic-triangle-complementation/current_inputs/SOURCE_OWNER.md:41:| P112 `main.tex`, initial sections and stated update | Synchronous outdegree-based score-upset reversal, not a lexicographic monochromatic triangle. Its mature tournament-reversal neighbourhood is still subtracted. |
papers/203-monochromatic-triangle-complementation/current_inputs/SOURCE_OWNER.md:42:| P152 `main.tex`, definition and source-boundary table | Established stochastic imbalanced-triad dynamics on a triangular book; choose one active sign-product-negative page and flip one random edge. MCT complements three edges deterministically, tests equality rather than sign product, and uses all pairs on the full labelled carrier. P152's reflected count quotient and Chebyshev inverse do not provide the MCT no-return or Johnson-family fibre. |
